    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class in the project, and it passes. The build is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI replaced the level rules with the specified points system.\n\n**What changed:**\n\n1. **`src/main/java/.../model/Owner.java`** \u2014 the derived-field logic lives on the `Owner` entity (alongside `getMembershipNumber`, `getCheckDigit`, `getTenureDays`, etc.), so I kept it there, split into two single-responsibility getters:\n   - `getMembershipPoints()` \u2014 computes the score from the owner's own fields: `+2` email present, `+1` `namesakeCount == 0`, `+2` household of 3+ (this now uses the previously-unused `householdSize` field), `+3` tenure over 365 days.\n   - `getMembershipLevel()` \u2014 a pure mapping from points to level: `1` (0\u20131), `2` (2\u20133), `3` (4\u20135), `4` (6+). It delegates to `getMembershipPoints()` rather than duplicating the factor logic.\n   - Renamed the tenure constant and added a `HOUSEHOLD_SIZE_FOR_POINTS` constant, matching the existing constant style.\n\n2. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 since `OwnerDto` is generated from the spec and MapStruct maps by getter name, I added a `membershipPoints` property (so the new getter is serialized) and updated `membershipLevel` (range now 1\u20134, description rewritten to describe the points mapping). Both fields are returned on the owner response.\n\nThe existing consumer `OwnerAuditor` still logs `membershipLevel` unchanged and needed no edits.\n\n**Verification:** `./mvnw test` \u2192 BUILD SUCCESS, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`. The acceptance test confirms a fresh owner with an email and no namesake scores `membershipPoints=3` \u2192 `membershipLevel=2`.",
