    "probe_text": "Here is the complete, ordered sequence of validations and side-effects applied when creating an owner via **`POST /api/owners`** (handled by `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`).\n\n## Before the controller body runs\n\n1. **Authorization** \u2014 `@PreAuthorize(\"hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)\")` requires role `ROLE_OWNER_ADMIN` (only enforced when `petclinic.security.enable=true`). *Validation.*\n2. **Bean Validation on the request DTO** (`@Valid @RequestBody OwnerFieldsDto`) \u2014 runs before the method body:\n   - `firstName`: `@NotNull`, `@Pattern` (letters, up to 3 words), `@Size(1..30)`\n   - `lastName`: `@NotNull`, `@Pattern` (+ optional trailing `.`), `@Size(1..30)`\n   - `address`: `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..255)`\n   - `city`: `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..80)`\n   - `postcode` (optional): `@Pattern(\"^[0-9]{4}$\")`\n   - `telephone`: `@NotNull`, `@Pattern`, `@Size(1..20)`\n   - `email` (optional): `@Size(max 255)`, `@Email`\n   - Failure \u2192 **400** (`MethodArgumentNotValidException`). *Validation.*\n\n## Inside the controller method (in this exact order)\n\n3. **`AddressNormalizer.normalize`** \u2014 mutates the DTO's `address`: trims, collapses whitespace, uppercases, expands `ST\u2192STREET`, `RD\u2192ROAD`, `AVE\u2192AVENUE`. *Side-effect (on the DTO).*\n4. **`OwnerFieldsValidator.findMissingFields`** \u2014 checks firstName/lastName/address/city/telephone are non-blank; if any missing \u2192 **400** (`MissingOwnerFieldsException`). *Validation.*\n5. **`ownerMapper.toOwner(dto)`** \u2014 maps DTO into a new `Owner` entity (ignores `id`, `pets`). *Side-effect (object creation).*\n6. **`PostcodeValidator.isValidForCity`** \u2014 postcode's region must match the city's region (blank postcode allowed); mismatch \u2192 **400** (`InvalidPostcodeException`). *Validation.*\n7. **`clinicService.countOwnersByCity`** \u2014 if `>= 50` (`MAX_OWNERS_PER_CITY`) \u2192 **409** (`CityCapacityExceededException`). *Validation (DB query).*\n8. **`RegistrationDatePolicy.isAfterServerDate`** \u2014 if registration date is after today \u2192 **400** (`FutureRegistrationDateException`). *Validation.*\n9. **`RegistrationDatePolicy.effectiveDate`** + **`clinicService.countOwnersRegisteredOn`** \u2014 if that day already has `>= 100` (`MAX_OWNERS_PER_DAY`) \u2192 **429** (`DailyOwnerLimitExceededException`). *Validation (DB query).*\n10. **`TelephoneNormalizer.normalize`** \u2014 mutates `telephone` to E.164 form (default country `+61`, drops leading `0`, enforces 8\u201315 digits); failure \u2192 **400** (`InvalidTelephoneException`). *Side-effect + validation.*\n11. **`EmailNormalizer.normalize`** \u2014 mutates `email` (blank\u2192null, else trimmed lowercase). *Side-effect.*\n12. **`DisposableEmailValidator.isDisposable`** \u2014 blocks `mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com` \u2192 **400** (`DisposableEmailException`). *Validation.*\n13. **`HouseholdIdGenerator.generate`** \u2014 sets `householdId` (SHA-256 prefix of lastName|postcode, or null if no postcode). *Side-effect.*\n14. **`declaredHouseholdMember`** set from the DTO's `sharesHousehold` flag. *Side-effect.*\n15. **`clinicService.isHouseholdDuplicate`** \u2014 only if *not* a declared household member; if an existing owner shares the householdId \u2192 **409** (`DuplicateIdentityException`). *Validation (DB query).*\n\n## Persistence \u2014 `clinicService.saveOwner` (`@Transactional`)\n\n16. For a new owner, mutates the entity before persisting:\n    - sets `customerCode` (via `CustomerCodeGenerator`, if null)\n    - sets `namesakeCount` (via `NamesakeCounter`, DB query)\n    - sets `householdSize` (via `HouseholdMemberCounter`, DB query)\n    - runs `PossibleDuplicateDetector` (unless declared member) and sets `possibleDuplicate` / `possibleDuplicateOf`\n    *Side-effects.*\n17. **`ownerRepository.save`** \u2192 `em.persist` (insert). *Side-effect (DB write).*\n18. **`Owner.@PrePersist resolveRegistrationDate()`** fires at persist time \u2014 finalizes `registrationDate` (defaults null\u2192today, rolls weekends forward to Monday). *Side-effect.*\n\n## After the transaction\n\n19. **`ownerAuditor.ownerCreated`** \u2014 logs `id, customerCode, registrationDate, membershipLevel` to the `AUDIT` logger (not transactional). *Side-effect.*\n20. **`toOwnerDtoWithBulkSignupWarning`** \u2014 maps to `OwnerDto` and runs **another** `countOwnersRegisteredOn` query, setting `bulkSignupWarning` if today's count `> 80`. *Side-effect (DB query).*\n21. Sets `Location: /api/owners/{id}` header and returns **201 Created**. *Side-effect.*\n\n**Notes on ordering/design worth flagging:**\n- The controller has **no `@Transactional`**, so each `clinicService.*` call is a separate transaction \u2014 the pre-save count checks (steps 7, 9, 15) are not atomic with the insert, leaving TOCTOU race windows on the city/daily caps and duplicate check.\n- The DTO's `@Pattern` for telephone (step 2) and the `Owner` entity's own `@Pattern(\"^\\\\+[0-9]{8,15}$\")` describe *different* formats; the entity constraint is satisfied only after `TelephoneNormalizer` (step 10) rewrites the value.\n- `AddressNormalizer` (step 3) runs *before* the missing-fields check but *after* Bean Validation, so it mutates the already-validated address."
